WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:05.339
Chances are, most moviegoers didn't expect
to get their hearts broken by Jurassic World:

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:06.649
Fallen Kingdom.

00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:11.099
After all, this is standard popcorn action
fare, featuring deadly dinos, bad decisions

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:13.370
by the humans, and a whole lot of fun.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:17.840
But there was one scene that caused many fans
of the hugely popular adventure series to

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.950
choke up and walk away rather traumatized.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.730
Click away now if you're still avoiding spoilers,
or you might be traumatized yourself…

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.710
"You're the one who made me come here.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.840
I'll be alright."

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.130
The scene that seems to have gutted a lot
of moviegoers features Chris Pratt's Owen,

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:37.780
Bryce Dallas Howard's Claire, and Justice
Smith's Franklin escaping Isla Nublar just

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.670
seconds before the island's active volcano
destroys the defunct theme park.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:46.000
While some of the dinosaurs have been transported
from the island by Ken Wheatley's salvage

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.500
operation, our trio of heroes spot a helpless
Brachiosaurus who has been left behind as

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:54.440
the clouds of smoke billow around and eventually
engulf the moaning animal.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.329
Those who caught Fallen Kingdom in theaters
have since flocked to social media to share

00:00:58.329 --> 00:00:59.980
their grief over the scene.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:04.470
As one user put it: "Not to be dramatic but
I would die for that Brachiosaurus in Jurassic

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.470
World."

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:09.040
Another fan admitted that he was "lying in
bed thinking about THAT Brachiosaurus" long

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.580
after Fallen Kingdom's credits rolled.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:16.160
One woman compared her outrage over the Brachiosaurus'
demise to the way some fans felt after seeing

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.720
Star Wars: The Last Jedi, and another was
left completely crushed after witnessing the

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.860
emotionally distressing sequence and wrote:
"All I wanna do is cry.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.610
And all I want is a giant hug right now.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.240
That scene had no business ruining my emotional
life.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.240
I'm scarred."

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.860
Last but not least, at least one user had
reached the bargaining stage of grief over

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.860
the scene, writing: "I'd be less emotional
if [Chris Pratt's] character was eaten by

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:43.920
an Allosaurus which is then eaten by a Tyrannosaurus
Rex which is then eaten by a Mosasaurus."

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.140
Hey, there's still another sequel in the works,
so who knows?

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.090
That very well could still happen.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.480
"Not yet, kid."

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.730
The brachiosaurus has always been among the
friendliest members of the dino kingdom in

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.800
the series, after being introduced in 1993's
Jurassic Park.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:02.020
"Just think of it as kind of a big cow."

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:06.830
So it's especially heartbreaking to watch
this gentle giant collapse under such excruciating

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:11.920
circumstances, and director Juan Antonio Bayona
has admitted to capitalizing on the nostalgia

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.780
factor associated with the species.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.260
He even played a sadder version of the Jurassic
Park melody over the scene to represent what

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:21.780
he called "the ending of a dream that started
25 years ago."

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.469
"It was all a lie!"

00:02:23.469 --> 00:02:27.519
While we dry our eyes and try to scrub away
the image of the Brachiosaurus that's now

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:31.939
burned into our brain, we're left with one
hope: that the Jurassic World team doesn't

00:02:31.939 --> 00:02:35.079
pull a stunt like this again in the third
movie.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.060
Dinosaurs are people, too …

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.960
"Oh God.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.240
OH GOD!"

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.240
"Tah-dah!"

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:43.800
Thanks for watching!

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.920
